A||||8||Denise||Timing on 2.8 and gas milage||||1||
Z||000000||Denise||05-22-2000||12:56 PM||||the gas milage in my rebult jasper 2.8 is pretty good but, can the milage be inproved any?  retard the ignition? anything else? Cat is new too. with the 5 spd it never pings not even in 5th gear going up hill. <BR>Thanks <BR>Denise Philly PA.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||05-22-2000||01:06 PM||||<BR>A quick and cheap way to make sure you are getting all the mpg you can get is to make sure you have a tuneup. When was the last time you had this done?<P>Things to change, plugs, plug wires, distruibutor cap, rotor, pcv valve, fuel filter, air cleaner, and drive belts.<P>Also make sure you have the tires running at the proper inflation. Under inflated tires cause premature tire wear and reduce your mpg.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-22-2000||06:46 PM||||Retard the ignition? Sheesh man, it's only gas.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||05-22-2000||07:04 PM||||Make sure you have a tune up, chande the oil frequently a lot of TLC. I'm not sure milage improves as you retard the timing.  I go by factory specs.  The best way to improve gas milage is the way you drive and the terrain you drive in.<P>I can obtain 30+mpg on the highway using cruise control, or just keeping up with traffic flow.  I can also get much less maybe 20mpg, when I drive the car hard.<P>When you drive the car hard things break and you do use the gas.  At $1.50+ a gallon, you'll need $ for repairs and gas.  And as you read this forum, many of the Fiero hot rodders don't have money for either.  <P>You paid big bucks for a Jasper engine, baby it and it will last a long time.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000004||DRH||05-22-2000||07:26 PM||||Hi Denise, Welcome!!!<P>I'm with Old Lar. Other than making sure everything is up to par (plugs, cap, wires, fuel injectors) the best way to improve MPG is driving style. If retarding the timing would improve gas milage significantly I believe GM would have done it that way to begin with.<P>I have an 88 Formula, V6 5 spd. I get as high as 30 on the highway, low to mid 20s around town, and "not so good" autocrossing.<P><BR>David.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Denise||05-22-2000||07:38 PM||||Hi Guys thanks for the input on the Gas Mileage.  yes it's well tuned Egr is working well also. had a code 32 awhile back,  the Solinoid was bad.  Me drive hard? &lt;evil grin&gt; Lets just say I don't try to smoke the tires.  I do get good Mileage on a trip. around town it's low becasue I have a heavy foot.  <BR>Thanks for the input!  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||05-22-2000||08:58 PM||||Welcome Denise to our "Fiero nuthouse"! Are you Delvalfiero's at egroups? Notice your quite active with Fiero events and hope you'll end up spending as much time here as the list <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000007||Shiner||05-22-2000||10:35 PM||||Denise,<BR> I get pretty horrific gas mileage in my '87GT getrag.  On the highway, that low 5th gear really keeps the revs down, so the mileage is pretty good.  Around town (well, on the backroads where I live), I think I have hit the sub-10mpg marker.  My father and I were discussing this, and the only thing we could think of to attribute the low-mpg to was wieght.  This ain't no 1900lb Honda Civic.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||05-23-2000||01:41 AM||||Shiner,<P>You should be getting better than that. You would really have to run it hard to get less than 10 MPG. I get over 20 with quite a bit of stop and go driving. I don't run wide open but I don't baby it either. <P>You may have something wrong??? Or a REALLY heavy foot?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
